# The launcher's search and the Settings window (0.0.5g): typing in the
# search box finds an application; Settings changes the accent colour, the
# wallpaper and the window-border effect; the screen resolution changes and
# changes back, with the desktop and the shell still working at each size.
# Coordinates assume the 1280x800 test display and the Settings window
# opening centred (frame at 290,92, 700x560).
bga: display adapter
gui: desktop up at 1280x800
cerberus kernel shell
# Click the taskbar's search box, type, and take the first match with Enter.
!mouseto 150 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!key set
!wait 1
!screenshot build/settings-1.png
# Appearance: the Aurora wallpaper and the teal accent.
!mouseto 680 292
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 769 185
!button left down
!button left up
# Window borders: the Chase effect, 3 pixels wide.
!mouseto 370 193
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 510 223
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 636 395
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.7
!screenshot build/settings-2.png
# Display: down to 1024x768.
!mouseto 340 233
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 634 215
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 1.5
gui: resolution changed to 1024x768
!screenshot build/settings-3.png
# The terminal still takes input at the new size.
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key ticks
!wait 1
ticks=
# And back up to 1280x800.
!mouseto 600 107
!button left down
!button left up
!mouseto 864 215
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 1.5
gui: resolution changed to 1280x800
!screenshot build/settings-4.png
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key gui
!wait 1
frames
# The same from the keyboard: the shell's `resolution` command.
!key resolution 1440 900
!wait 1.5
gui: resolution changed to 1440x900
!key resolution
!wait 1
resolution: 1440x900
!key resolution 99 99
!wait 1
resolution: this display cannot show 99x99
